{
  "metadata": {
    "L": 3,
    "K": 3,
    "d": 4,
    "description": "3-Hop-SwitchVariance-v2: H=3,K=3 (27 leaves). Two deliberately opposite specialists at arm_000 (PREFILL_FAST: cheap per-input-token, linear+quadratic; expensive per-output-token) and arm_222 (DECODE_FAST: mirror opposite). Two extreme, hand-designed contexts -- CTX_IN (n=990,m=2, ~495:1 input:output ratio) and CTX_OUT (n=2,m=990, ~1:495) -- are each the clear best match for one specialist and the clear worst match for the other. At rel_t=0.01 (T/100, an early switch matching Hou et al.'s convention), the two specialists' theta vectors are SWAPPED (not re-randomized) -- CTX_IN's best/worst leaves exactly reverse, and so does CTX_OUT's. All other leaves and contexts are generic/unspecialized (jittered average of the two specialists), needing no special design."
  },
